WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you so much.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
Thanks.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.269 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's great to be here.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:07.107
I grew up in New York City
and I went to college here, too.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:10.076 size:75% position:38%
I went to Juilliard.
I played the viola.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.779 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you don't know
what a viola is, I'll tell you

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like a violin
but a little bigger

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
and nobody cares.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.359 size:78% position:39%
I like telling people
I went to Juilliard

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:31.097
because they act impressed
and then I act modest...

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
...and I love that.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.836
They're like, "Whoa, Juilliard."
I'm like, "Eh, it's nothing.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"Wow, humble and talented.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:42.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Yes."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:45.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I am perfect."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.313 line:92%
It's annoying when sometimes

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone hasn't heard
of Juilliard.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:56.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause then I just have
to politely explain to the

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.124 size:78% position:39% line:92%
that it's a big deal.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.527 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"Oh, what's Juilliard?"

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"Oh, it's just, you know,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:06.766 line:92%
one of the best music schools.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.668
They're like, "Oh, music?
My niece plays violin."

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"Yeah, she wouldn't get in."

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:18.144 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I was 9,
I went to soccer camp,

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.149
and that was a nightmare
'cause I was bad at sports

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I knew
I was particularly bad,

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.153 size:75% position:38% line:92%
because at the camp,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
everyone would call me
a "good sport."

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's where you're
just so used to losing

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:37.130 size:75% position:38%
and it gets mistaken
for a good attitude.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Well, we lost again."

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
The coach is like,
"This kid gets it."

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.572 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.606 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But I'm competitive,

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I liked being called
a good anything.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, "good sport,"
I was like, "All right.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.747 line:92%
I will be the best sport."

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.952
And at the end of the summer
they gave out these awards

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they announced
the sportsmanship award.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:05.992
And I was fully expecting
to get this, and I didn't.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.660 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Some other loser did.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
Apparently, this quiet gir
named Jenny had been muttering

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.434 line:92%
"Good game" the whole summer

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:17.871 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I went up to her after.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Hey, congratulations."

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like,
"You should've gotten it."

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Oh, you're good, Jenny."

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:26.713 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jenny...
[ Scoffs ]

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.484 line:92%
I was with my friend recently,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.819 size:81% position:41%
and she said something
kind of weird to me.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like, "Isabel,
you have resting sad face.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.491 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, no.
It's active."

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.266 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't smile a lot
in my everyday life.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have kind of a goofy smile
I get self-conscious.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's fun
when I get that cat call, like

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, baby, smile."
"Okay." [ Growls ]

00:02:55.308 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like, "Never mind.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:04.717 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I have been sad.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
I recently
went through a break-up.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm scared
to fall in love again now

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
because here's what I learne
about love, all right?

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Love is the only thing that,
when you lose it,

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
you doubt it ever existed
in the first place.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:18.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one ever loses their keys
and they're like,

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, maybe
there never were any keys.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't even know."

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:31.044 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:35.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Maybe I've just been
letting myself in with lies.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:41.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been trying
to get out of the house more

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.824 line:92%
I was in a coffee shop recently,

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I saw a mother
with her baby.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went up to them,
and I was like, "Excuse me

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:52.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's so cute."
And the mom said, "Thank you,"

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
taking the compliment
for the baby.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
That made me think,
"I wish I had my mom with me

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.110
to take all the compliment
I receive in public today.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
That'd be nice.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.381
Some guy walks by me, he's like,
"Damn, she's sexy."

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.450 line:92%
My mom's like, "Thank you.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.451 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.020 size:78% position:39%
"Isabel, the nice man
wants to bang you.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:18.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
Say thank you."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love my mom.
I do.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.628 line:92%
We have a good relationship.

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:28.401
My mom recently informed me that
I breastfed till I was 3.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.769 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Yeah, Mom, I remember."

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:40.813 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.383 line:92%
"I was in preschool, yeah.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kids would be like,
"You wanna trade lunches?"

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.586 line:92%
I was like, "My mom just left.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.521 line:92%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you!
I'm Isabel Hagen.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.624 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.127 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.161 line:92%
-I have to fist-bump you.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.563 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I can't shake hands.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
Isabel Hagen!
Oh, my goodness!

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.402 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
For more,
